course: dictionary
lesson: 11269
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. «Wrestling» is a good example. In a sports lesson it names a sport where two people hold each other and try to pin the other to the ground.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «The Olympic Games began in 776 BC at Olympia, with running, wrestling, the discus and chariot races» has a list of sports, so wrestling must be a sport here. But if someone says «I am wrestling with a maths problem», the word means struggling hard, not fighting.
explain: Test your meaning in the sentence. Swap in «struggling» or «fighting» and ask: does it still make sense? If it does, you have probably found the right meaning. Always check the clues first, because the same word can change its meaning from one sentence to the next.
fact: Wrestling is a sport in which two people hold each other and try to throw or pin the other to the ground, without punching.
fact: As a verb, wrestle can mean struggling with someone or something, or struggling hard with a problem.
fact: Professional wrestling on TV is a show with planned moves and storylines. It is more acting than real competition.
fact: Wrestling is one of the oldest sports. It was part of the ancient Olympic Games.
fact: TV wrestling moves are performed by trained stunt athletes and must never be copied at home.
exercise: «Cubs play constantly, chasing tails and wrestling.» In this sentence, wrestling means | Watching a film on TV | *Sleeping in the sun | Play-fighting by holding and pushing each other | Cooking dinner for the family
exercise: Maya says, «I am wrestling with my homework.» What does wrestling mean here? | Eating a big dinner | *Struggling hard to get it done | Holding a friend on the floor | Watching a wrestling show
exercise: Professional wrestling on TV is a show with planned moves and storylines. What is it more like? | A quiz show | A cookery lesson | A real Olympic final | *More acting than real competition
test: Find and copy one word from «The Olympic Games began in 776 BC at Olympia, with running, wrestling, the discus and chariot races» that names a sport. | Zeus | honour | *wrestling | Olympia
test: Ella says, «Wrestling on TV is always real fighting.» Is she right? | *No, TV wrestling has planned moves and is more acting than sport | Yes, every TV wrestling match is a real fight | Yes, but only at the Olympics | No, because wrestling is a quiet game with no moves
exam: «Big jaws and horns are mostly for wrestling rivals.» What does this suggest the animals use their jaws and horns for? | Cooking food for their young | Reading the wood they live in | *Holding and pushing rivals in a fight | Singing to attract a mate
